link-zstd

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Compress lines between machines with zstd: a dialing core offers it in its framed hello, a core that can take it says so in the reply, and from there each direction is one zstd stream for the life of the connection, flushed whenever its sender has nothing more queued, so typing is never held back. Older cores ignore the offer and the line stays plain. [link] in config.toml sets compression (zstd or none) and level (1 to 19, default 3).
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream herdr-core compresses lines between machines.
